content:         1→<informal_theorem>
        2→Prove the lemma `Xm_zero_in_G`, whose Lean statement is fixed below. It is one step in the proof of the following result; the Lean definitions in the Setting encode that result's objects and rules, and the earlier lemmas given there may be used as facts.
        3→
        4→Setting:
        5→Let $\mathbb{C}$ denote the set of complex numbers, let $\mathbb{N}$ denote the set of natural numbers.
        6→Let $c(j)$ denote  the coefficient of $q^j$ in the  modular function
        7→
        8→$$J(q)=\sum_{j\geq -1}c(j)q^j= {1 \over q}  + 196884 q + 21493760 q^2 + 864299970 q^3  + \cdots$$
        9→
       10→so that $c(-1) = 1,\ c(0) = 0,\ c(1) = 196884, \dots$
       11→
       12→Define an index set:
       13→
       14→$$E=  \left\{(\ell,j,k)\mid j\in\mathbb{N},\, 1 \leq k\leq c(j),\, 0\leq \ell<j \right\}$$
       15→
       16→Define a complex number: $$c_{\ell j} := (-1)^{\ell+1} \binom{j-1}{\ell} \, (\ell+1)(j-\ell)$$
       17→
       18→Let $\mathcal{X}$ be the set of symbols
       19→$$\mathcal{X} :=\{H_1(s), H_2(s), X_{-1}(u),  Y_{-1}(u), X_{\ell,jk}(u), Y_{\ell,jk}(u) \mid$$ 
       20→$$\qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad\qquad \qquad \qquad \qquad s\in \mathbb{C}^\times, u\in \mathbb{C}, (\ell,j,k)\in E\}.$$
       21→Let $F(\mathcal{X})$ denote the free group on~$\mathcal{X}$.
       22→
       23→We  call  $X_{-1}(u)$, $Y_{-1}(u)$, $X_{\ell,jk}(u)$ and $Y_{\ell,jk}(u)$ {\it unipotent generators}.
       24→
       25→We define $\mathcal{R}\subseteq F(\mathcal{X})$  and additional symbols $ \widetilde{w}_{-1}(s)$ and   $\widetilde{w}_{\ell,jk}(s)$ as follows, for all $s,t\in \mathbb{C}^\times$, $u,v\in \mathbb{C}$, $(\ell,j,k),(m,p,q) \in E$.\\
       26→
       27→\begingroup\allowdisplaybreaks
       28→\begin{align*}
       29→\tag{Re:0} 
       30→  \widetilde{w}_{-1}(s) &:= X_{-1}(s) Y_{-1}\left(-s^{-1} \right) X_{-1}(s), \\ \widetilde{w}_{-1} &:= \widetilde{w}_{-1}(1),\\
       31→\tag{Im:0}
       32→  \widetilde{w}_{\ell,jk}(s) &:= X_{\ell,jk}\left({s}\right) Y_{\ell,jk}\left(\frac{-s^{-1}}{{c_{\ell j}}}\right) 
       33→  X_{\ell,jk}\left({s}\right),\\  \widetilde{w}_{\ell,jk} &:= \widetilde{w}_{\ell,jk}(1),\\
       34→\intertext{Relations that define a subgroup $\mathrm{GL}_2(-1)$:}
       35→\tag{H:1a}
       36→   H_1(s)H_1(t)&=H_1(st),\\
       37→\tag{H:1b}
       38→   H_2(s)H_2(t)&=H_2(st),\\
       39→\tag{H:2}
       40→    H_1(s)H_2(t)&=H_2(t)H_1(s),\\
       41→\tag{Re:1a}
       42→   X_{-1}(u)X_{-1}(v)&=X_{-1}(u+v),\\
       43→\tag{Re:1b}
       44→   Y_{-1}(u)Y_{-1}(v)&=Y_{-1}(u+v),\\
       45→\tag{Re:2}
